# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The meta-repo tracks almost nothing: four submodule POINTERS, the ecosystem
# registry, the orchestration scripts and the docs. Everything else belongs to a
# submodule and is ignored by that submodule's own .gitignore.
#
# Nothing here ignores the submodule directories themselves — git tracks those
# as gitlink entries, and an ignore rule on one would silently stop the pointer
# being recorded, which is the failure that makes a fresh clone come up empty.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/

# Never a secret in the meta-repo. Per-system env files live inside each
# submodule, ignored there.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Node — the meta-repo has no dependencies, but a stray install should not be
# committed if someone adds one.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local scratch
*.local
/tmp/
/scratch/
